---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  path="/terms"
  description="Trade terms for SUP Stocklot Direct: AS-IS liquidation sale, no brand warranty, territory resale restrictions, 30–50% non-refundable deposit, inspection sign-off = delivery, FOB Qingdao / EXW, 3–5 business day dispatch, B2B only."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-50 sm:text-4xl">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Applies to all stocklots sold by {SITE.name}. Last updated {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' })}.</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-slate-300">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">1. Scope — B2B only</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          We sell exclusively to businesses (importers, distributors, rental operators, retail chains). Every lot
          carries a minimum order quantity ({SITE.moqPolicy}). We do not sell to consumers, and we do not split lots
          below the stated MOQ.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">2. Sold AS-IS — no brand warranty</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          All stock is liquidation inventory (cancelled orders, surplus production, cosmetic seconds) and is sold
          <strong class="text-slate-100">AS-IS, WHERE-IS</strong>. There is <strong class="text-slate-100">no brand
          warranty</strong>: no manufacturer warranty claims, guarantee cards or after-sales service from the original
          factory are included or implied. Product titles on this site are de-branded engineering descriptions; original
          branding is neither marketed nor warranted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">3. What we do guarantee</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>Honest grading: Grade A = brand-new cancelled-order/surplus; Grade B = cosmetic seconds (100% airtight).</li>
          <li>Every board passes a <strong class="text-slate-100">72-hour inflated pressure test</strong> ({SITE.qcProtocol.pressure}, pressure drop {SITE.qcProtocol.maxDrop}) before dispatch.</li>
          <li>Accurate manifests: quantities, carton dimensions, gross/net weights and accessory lists per lot.</li>
          <li>The goods conform to the description of the specific lot confirmed on your pro-forma invoice.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">4. Prices, incoterms &amp; payment</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Prices are quoted in USD, {SITE.incoterms}. Tiered pricing is per lot and based on the confirmed quantity
          on the pro-forma invoice.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-slate-100">Payment: {SITE.paymentTerms}</strong> Stock is only allocated once the
          deposit is received. Availability and prices can change without notice until an order is confirmed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">5. Deposit, allocation hold &amp; default</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          The 30–50% deposit locks your allocation and holds it for <strong class="text-slate-100">{SITE.allocationHoldDays}
          days</strong> from the pro-forma invoice date. The deposit is <strong class="text-slate-100">non-refundable</strong>:
          during the hold we decline other buyers on the reserved goods, and the costs of that are yours if you walk
          away. If the hold expires without the balance payment or a mutually agreed extension, the allocation is
          released back to the market and the deposit is forfeited. If we become unable to supply a confirmed and
          deposited lot before dispatch, you may switch to an equivalent lot or receive a full refund of amounts paid.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">6. Inspection — sign-off is delivery</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Buyers are welcome to appoint a third-party inspection agency (SGS, BV, TÜV or equivalent) at our Qingdao
          warehouse before dispatch, and/or container-loading supervision. Inspection fees and agency costs are borne
          by the buyer. We provide carton access, sampling and loading supervision. Personal visits can be arranged
          via WhatsApp.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-slate-100">Your inspection sign-off (or the sign-off of your appointed agency)
          constitutes acceptance and delivery of the goods</strong> in the condition inspected. Issues visible,
          observable or reasonably discoverable at inspection cannot be raised as claims afterwards. Risk in the goods
          passes to the buyer at the delivery point defined by the agreed incoterm (FOB: on board at Qingdao; EXW:
          made available at our warehouse).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">7. Dispatch &amp; allocation</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Confirmed orders dispatch within <strong class="text-slate-100">{SITE.dispatchWindow}</strong>. Lots are
          allocated strictly in order of payment confirmation. Until your deposit is received, the lot remains on the
          market and may sell out — low-stock lots move in days.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">8. Claims</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Because goods are sold AS-IS, post-delivery claims are limited to quantity discrepancies against the
          packing list and damage demonstrably caused before container sealing (documented at loading). Report such
          issues within 7 days of container unsealing, with photo/video evidence. There are no returns of sold
          stocklots.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">9. Territory &amp; resale restrictions</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Some lots carry territory restrictions agreed with the original brand or seller (for example: not for
          resale in a specific country or market channel). Where a restriction applies, it is stated on the
          pro-forma invoice and acknowledged by the buyer before the deposit. Buyers are responsible for complying
          with any restriction attached to their purchase, for their own import-market regulations (see the
          <a class="text-teal-300 hover:text-teal-200" href="/shipping/">compliance notes</a>), and for not
          marketing or reselling the goods in a way that infringes third-party trademark or IP rights. We sell
          de-branded physical goods; how you list and market them is your responsibility.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">10. Neutral export packing</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Goods ship in neutral export-grade cartons: no original brand marks, marketing inserts or barcodes on the
          outer packaging. Ship-to marks are applied per buyer instructions. Inner manual/label replacement can be
          discussed per lot before the deposit. Original branded packaging material, where it exists, is disposed of
          and never shipped.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">11. Gated portal material</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Access to the branded inventory portal (packing lists, barcode ranges, branded photos) is granted to
          verified business buyers and may be revoked at any time. Portal material is confidential, provided for
          purchase evaluation only, and may not be republished or redistributed. Screenshotting and sharing portal
          material with third parties is a breach of the access grant.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">12. Governing terms &amp; contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          The full bilingual Terms of Sale, IP Indemnification &amp; Liability Waiver governing any transaction is
          provided to verified buyers inside the inventory portal and applies alongside these terms. Questions on any
          clause? Message the sales desk on WhatsApp ({SITE.whatsappDisplay}) or email
          <a class="text-teal-300 hover:text-teal-200" href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
          before placing an order.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 rounded-2xl border border-amber-400/30 bg-amber-400/5 p-6 text-sm text-slate-300">
      <p class="font-semibold text-amber-300">Plain-English summary</p>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        You get honestly graded, pressure-tested liquidation stock at a fraction of regular wholesale. In exchange:
        no brand warranty, no returns, no factory after-sales. Your deposit locks the lot and is non-refundable.
        Inspect before dispatch — we encourage it — but your inspection sign-off is final acceptance. Respect any
        territory restrictions on the lot you buy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
